{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"callAsyncJavaScript"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"functionBody"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arguments","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Any","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"] = [:], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"webView","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)WKWebView","text":"WKWebView","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"completionHandler","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (@","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultO","text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Any","kind":"keyword"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8BrazeKit0A0C13WebViewBridgeO20ScriptMessageHandlerC5ErrorO","text":"Error","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/WebViewBridge\/ScriptMessageHandler\/Error","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil)","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"functionBody","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The JavaScript string to use as the function body. This method treats"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the string as an anonymous JavaScript function body and calls it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the named arguments in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"arguments"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter."}]}]},{"name":"arguments","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary of the arguments to pass to the function call. Each key in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dictionary corresponds to the name of an argument in the functionBody"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string, and the value of that key is the value to use during the evaluation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the code. Supported value types are "},{"code":"NSNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"NSString","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"NSArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"NSNull","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". All items in an array or dictionary must also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be one of the supported types."}]}]},{"name":"webView","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The web view in which the JavaScript function is executed. The web view must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implement the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/WebViewBridge\/ScriptMessageHandler"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"completionHandler","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A handler block to execute when script evaluation finishes. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method calls your block whether script evaluation completes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successfully or fails. The block has no return value and takes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following parameter:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"result: The result of the script evaluation, or an error object that contains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information about the problem that occurred. If your function body doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"return an explicit value, WebKit passes ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to your completion handler on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success. If your function explicitly returns null, WebKit returns that value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSNull","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function is a backport of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView.callAsyncJavaScript(_:arguments:in:completionHandler:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. It relies on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the script message handler to pass the result or error to the native side"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronously."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It differs from the WebKit method in the following ways:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No support for passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSDate"},{"type":"text","text":" as an argument."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Errors are not wrapped in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t format the string in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"functionBody"},{"text":" parameter as a function-like callable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object, as you would in pure JavaScript. Instead, put only the body of the function in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string. For example, the following string shows a valid function body that takes x, y, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"z arguments and returns a result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"js","code":["return x ? y : z"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your JavaScript code returns an object with a callable ","type":"text"},{"code":"then","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, the function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls that property on the resulting object and waits for its resolution. If resolution","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"succeeds, the function passes the resulting object to your completion handler. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolution fails, the function returns an error to your completion handler.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because this method calls your JavaScript code asynchronously, you can call "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"objects with a then property inside your function body. The following code example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"illustrates this technique."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"js","code":["var p = new Promise(function (f) {","  window.setTimeout(\"f(42)\", 1000);","});","await p;","return p;"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID"